1028
00:36:59,667 --> 00:37:01,307
- Beef noodle soup? - Where is the place?

1029
00:37:01,607 --> 00:37:05,176
If you cross the street...

1030
00:37:05,177 --> 00:37:06,177
(Embarrassed)

1031
00:37:06,178 --> 00:37:07,247
I know we have no shame.

1032
00:37:08,447 --> 00:37:09,677
But I had to ask.

1033
00:37:09,977 --> 00:37:11,616
There's a knife-cut noodle place.

1034
00:37:11,617 --> 00:37:14,717
Their beef noodle soup and dim sum are amazing.

1035
00:37:14,917 --> 00:37:16,017
That sounds good.

1036
00:37:16,287 --> 00:37:18,886
- I'm so sorry. - No, we had lots of fun.

1037
00:37:18,887 --> 00:37:21,126
- Thank you. - It was fun.

1038
00:37:21,127 --> 00:37:23,896
Really, why couldn't I do it?

1039
00:37:23,897 --> 00:37:25,166
The keyboards were so pretty.

1040
00:37:25,167 --> 00:37:26,827
I know, right? The keyboards were pretty.

1041
00:37:27,327 --> 00:37:29,567
I can't stop thinking about it.

1042
00:37:31,067 --> 00:37:32,207
It's such a bummer.

1043
00:37:32,637 --> 00:37:34,107
I feel empty.

1044
00:37:35,077 --> 00:37:37,777
And you still asked for lunch recommendations.

1045
00:37:38,907 --> 00:37:39,976
I had no shame, right?

1046
00:37:39,977 --> 00:37:41,176
(Jae Seok's hunger outweighed his shame.)

1047
00:37:41,177 --> 00:37:43,276
It was shameless of me, but still.

1048
00:37:43,277 --> 00:37:45,317
Getting recommendations in person...

1049
00:37:45,947 --> 00:37:48,317
- is the best, in my opinion. - True.

1050
00:37:48,687 --> 00:37:49,716
Let's go.

1051
00:37:49,717 --> 00:37:52,287
(Heading to the recommended knife-cut noodle place)

1052
00:37:53,627 --> 00:37:55,656
The cars crossed the line.

1053
00:37:55,657 --> 00:37:56,657
(Quite a crowd has gathered.)

1054
00:37:56,658 --> 00:37:59,366
- Turn to the left. - It's noon now.

1055
00:37:59,367 --> 00:38:00,927
Look at all the people.

1056
00:38:01,837 --> 00:38:05,237
(Current time,12pm, lunch hour in Gwanghwamun)

1057
00:38:06,537 --> 00:38:08,607
Coincidentally, it's lunchtime.

1058
00:38:09,677 --> 00:38:13,006
Many office workers are out to grab lunch.

1059
00:38:13,007 --> 00:38:14,076
(The office workers are getting lunch.)

1060
00:38:14,077 --> 00:38:15,077
Is this the place?

1061
00:38:16,047 --> 00:38:17,147
We're here.

1062
00:38:17,577 --> 00:38:18,986
- Where? - Right here.

1063
00:38:18,987 --> 00:38:20,547
- Is that the place? - There's a line.

1064
00:38:20,687 --> 00:38:22,387
(Disappointed)

1065
00:38:22,657 --> 00:38:24,856
- I don't think we can eat here. - Right?

1066
00:38:24,857 --> 00:38:27,627
This place must be popular.

1067
00:38:27,757 --> 00:38:30,097
We might have to wait for a good while.

1068
00:38:31,157 --> 00:38:32,166
You have to wait for a while.

1069
00:38:32,167 --> 00:38:33,267
Is that so?

1070
00:38:33,967 --> 00:38:35,336
We can't dine here.

1071
00:38:35,337 --> 00:38:37,137
Shall we leave? I don't think we'll get a table soon.

1072
00:38:38,837 --> 00:38:41,107
Let's go. We won't get a table anytime soon.

1073
00:38:41,477 --> 00:38:43,037
Knife-cut noodles would've been nice.

1074
00:38:43,737 --> 00:38:45,507
(Bummed out)

1075
00:38:45,747 --> 00:38:47,607
- There are so many people here. - For real.

1076
00:38:48,317 --> 00:38:50,017
(Glancing)

1077
00:38:50,317 --> 00:38:52,686
- That place looks good. - Jongno Sujebi?

1078
00:38:52,687 --> 00:38:53,746
(Spotted a sujebi place)

1079
00:38:53,747 --> 00:38:55,316
They even serve dakkalguksu.

1080
00:38:55,317 --> 00:38:56,557
It's pretty cool here too.

1081
00:38:56,617 --> 00:38:57,816
This way.

1082
00:38:57,817 --> 00:39:00,656
(They quickly switch lunch plans.)

1083
00:39:00,657 --> 00:39:01,897
- Hi. - Hi.

1084
00:39:02,457 --> 00:39:04,097
- Hi. - Hi.

1085
00:39:04,527 --> 00:39:07,397
- Potato jeon sounds nice. - Right?

1086
00:39:08,097 --> 00:39:09,737
- I like it here. - Same.

1087
00:39:10,567 --> 00:39:11,637
It's nice.

1088
00:39:12,067 --> 00:39:13,406
- It's... - Down I go.

1089
00:39:13,407 --> 00:39:14,466
(They sit at a corner table.)

1090
00:39:14,467 --> 00:39:15,477
I'm...

1091
00:39:15,877 --> 00:39:16,877
What would you like?

1092
00:39:17,477 --> 00:39:19,977
I would like su...

1093
00:39:21,647 --> 00:39:23,246
- Sujebi? - I'm deciding between...

1094
00:39:23,247 --> 00:39:24,887
spicy and regular.

1095
00:39:25,687 --> 00:39:28,087
- I'm getting dakkalguksu. - Me too.

1096
00:39:28,187 --> 00:39:29,416
I want dakkalguksu too.

1097
00:39:29,417 --> 00:39:32,386
- Three dakkalguksu. - I'll get the spicy one.

1098
00:39:32,387 --> 00:39:34,626
We got here just as...

1099
00:39:34,627 --> 00:39:36,857
- the lunch rush started. - I know, right?

1100
00:39:37,157 --> 00:39:38,827
It's right when...

1101
00:39:39,327 --> 00:39:40,967
office workers grab lunch.

1102
00:39:42,497 --> 00:39:44,237
We have to pay first. Jae Seok.

1103
00:39:44,907 --> 00:39:47,367
We should play a game first since we have to pay upfront.

1104
00:39:48,607 --> 00:39:50,537
Do we have to pay already?

1105
00:39:51,277 --> 00:39:52,906
We have to pay right away.

1106
00:39:52,907 --> 00:39:54,106
- What should we do? - Is that so?

1107
00:39:54,107 --> 00:39:55,347
Hold on. Which game should we play?

1108
00:39:56,317 --> 00:39:58,717
Why don't we chopstick-wrestle? It's been a while.

1109
00:39:59,187 --> 00:40:00,216
Wait. What is that?

1110
00:40:00,217 --> 00:40:01,687
Right. You hold the chopsticks.

1111
00:40:01,987 --> 00:40:03,556
(Please refer to the episode with Jee Seok Jin and Ji Jin Hee.)

1112
00:40:03,557 --> 00:40:05,727
You play it like the one-legged wrestling.

1113
00:40:05,787 --> 00:40:10,457
(You lose if your chopstick falls after hitting your opponent's.)

1114
00:40:10,697 --> 00:40:11,896
You're not really good at games.

1115
00:40:11,897 --> 00:40:13,396
- Let's play up or down, - Okay.

1116
00:40:13,397 --> 00:40:14,867
and the matching pair can play the first round.

1117
00:40:14,997 --> 00:40:16,197
- Let's do that. - And then, we play the final.

1118
00:40:16,767 --> 00:40:18,966
- Okay. Up or down. - Up or down. Up.

1119
00:40:18,967 --> 00:40:20,036
(Down or up?)

1120
00:40:20,037 --> 00:40:21,937
- Up or down. - Up or down. Up.

1121
00:40:22,377 --> 00:40:24,137
- Up or down. - Up or down. Up.

1122
00:40:24,637 --> 00:40:26,477
- Up or down. Hold on. - Up or down. Down.

1123
00:40:26,877 --> 00:40:29,047
- What's going on? - We're pairing up.

1124
00:40:29,177 --> 00:40:30,346
- Isn't it Fronts and Backs? - It is, but...

1125
00:40:30,347 --> 00:40:32,417
- What's with "up and down," then? - This is correct.

1126
00:40:32,617 --> 00:40:34,016
You know that up or down varies...

1127
00:40:34,017 --> 00:40:35,456
- by region. - Of course.

1128
00:40:35,457 --> 00:40:37,056
- Really? - I learned a variation.

1129
00:40:37,057 --> 00:40:38,986
- How do they play it in Jeju? - What? How?

1130
00:40:38,987 --> 00:40:40,787
It's sky and land

1131
00:40:42,227 --> 00:40:43,756
- Stop lying. - I'm serious.

1132
00:40:43,757 --> 00:40:45,427
Someone from Jeju Island taught me.

1133
00:40:46,697 --> 00:40:48,337
That's how they play it.

1134
00:40:48,897 --> 00:40:50,067
Let's break into pairs.

1135
00:40:51,907 --> 00:40:53,267
(She loses epically.)

1136
00:40:53,707 --> 00:40:54,766
Soo Bin.

1137
00:40:54,767 --> 00:40:57,107
(A winner's smile)

1138
00:40:57,307 --> 00:40:59,347
- Soo Bin. - Go ahead.

1139
00:40:59,647 --> 00:41:01,577
- You guys are so unfair. - I mean,

1140
00:41:02,017 --> 00:41:03,276
- the youngest is paying. - Goodness.

1141
00:41:03,277 --> 00:41:05,047
I'll take them and give you new ones.

1142
00:41:06,247 --> 00:41:09,057
Hey. Can I get a Coke?

1143
00:41:09,887 --> 00:41:11,316
You should've told me at once.

1144
00:41:11,317 --> 00:41:12,587
- I'll get a lemon-lime soda too. - What?

1145
00:41:12,687 --> 00:41:14,626
- Does anyone want a soda? - I'm good.

1146
00:41:14,627 --> 00:41:17,297
- Do you want it? You can't decide? - I'll...

1147
00:41:17,857 --> 00:41:19,097
I'll have a sip of yours.

1148
00:41:19,327 --> 00:41:21,637
- No. Get your own. - Are you going to drink it all?

1149
00:41:21,897 --> 00:41:23,537
- Just get Sprite. - Are you going to finish it?

1150
00:41:24,937 --> 00:41:26,537
- Thanks, Soo Bin. - Okay.

1151
00:41:27,137 --> 00:41:28,236
They don't have the zero one.

1152
00:41:28,237 --> 00:41:29,237
That's true.

1153
00:41:29,507 --> 00:41:30,606
Good.

1154
00:41:30,607 --> 00:41:32,476
(The youngest one sets kimchi on the table.)

1155
00:41:32,477 --> 00:41:33,907
(Gentle)

1156
00:41:35,517 --> 00:41:36,677
You're good with your hands.

1157
00:41:38,177 --> 00:41:39,647
- He's delicate. - Yes. He's good.

1158
00:41:40,647 --> 00:41:42,056
- Do it. - My knees hurt now.

1159
00:41:42,057 --> 00:41:44,516
- All schedules are done without it. - The spicy one.

1160
00:41:44,517 --> 00:41:46,286
- Thank you. - The spicy one looks good too.

1161
00:41:46,287 --> 00:41:48,696
(The spicy sujebi and dakkalguksu loaded with toppings)

1162
00:41:48,697 --> 00:41:50,057
Gosh. It looks good.

1163
00:41:50,627 --> 00:41:51,767
It must be hot.

1164
00:41:51,867 --> 00:41:52,996
Let me try it.

1165
00:41:52,997 --> 00:41:54,497
(He tries the dakkalguksu first.)

1166
00:41:56,197 --> 00:41:58,037
(He loves noodles.)

1167
00:41:59,907 --> 00:42:00,937
(Slurping)

1168
00:42:04,307 --> 00:42:07,147
(Seung Ho will fly out tonight.)

1169
00:42:07,347 --> 00:42:08,347
(Slurping)

1170
00:42:08,877 --> 00:42:09,877
(Slurping)

1171
00:42:10,247 --> 00:42:11,247
(Slurping)

1172
00:42:12,087 --> 00:42:14,547
(He's devouring the food before he leaves the country.)

1173
00:42:14,747 --> 00:42:15,856
It's delicious.

1174
00:42:15,857 --> 00:42:17,317
- It's so good. - Yes.

1175
00:42:18,217 --> 00:42:20,026
(Clapping)

1176
00:42:20,027 --> 00:42:21,727
What do you do in your free time, Soo Bin?

1177
00:42:22,627 --> 00:42:23,957
Me? I look after my niece.

1178
00:42:25,197 --> 00:42:26,467
I think you talked about her last time too.

1179
00:42:26,667 --> 00:42:27,667
I hang out with my friends or my niece.

1180
00:42:27,668 --> 00:42:31,096
I see her about 2 to 3 times a week.

1181
00:42:31,097 --> 00:42:32,606
- I see. - She made an appearance...

1182
00:42:32,607 --> 00:42:34,837
in "When the Phone Rings" as a baby.

1183
00:42:35,007 --> 00:42:36,977
- Really? - She's gotten much bigger now.

1184
00:42:37,577 --> 00:42:38,706
She's at such a cute age.

1185
00:42:38,707 --> 00:42:40,247
Yes. She's really cute.

1186
00:42:41,077 --> 00:42:42,947
She sings and dances.

1187
00:42:43,417 --> 00:42:44,546
It must be so adorable.

1188
00:42:44,547 --> 00:42:46,717
I didn't expect myself to adore her this much.

1189
00:42:46,847 --> 00:42:48,586
- Really? - In fact, I was...

1190
00:42:48,587 --> 00:42:50,456
You didn't care much about babies?

1191
00:42:50,457 --> 00:42:52,287
No. Because there weren't any babies around me before.

1192
00:42:52,357 --> 00:42:53,856
- So you didn't know. - I didn't.

1193
00:42:53,857 --> 00:42:55,626
Now, they're so adorable.

1194
00:42:55,627 --> 00:42:57,226
After becoming an aunt, I find all other babies...

1195
00:42:57,227 --> 00:42:58,797
- adorable. - You can see that now, right?

1196
00:42:58,997 --> 00:43:00,727
I adore kids in the first place.

1197
00:43:01,997 --> 00:43:03,097
Do you adore kids, Seung Ho?

1198
00:43:03,237 --> 00:43:05,166
- I love them. - Really?

1199
00:43:05,167 --> 00:43:07,667
So I wanted to have kids fast even when I was an athlete.

1200
00:43:08,167 --> 00:43:09,376
You were really good with kids.

1201
00:43:09,377 --> 00:43:10,977
- I saw you with Eun Seong. - Yes.

1202
00:43:12,047 --> 00:43:13,207
I was his favorite.

1203
00:43:13,877 --> 00:43:16,717
Then you must be good with kids.

1204
00:43:17,647 --> 00:43:18,747
Seriously, though.

1205
00:43:19,747 --> 00:43:20,917
I'm so full.

1206
00:43:21,487 --> 00:43:23,316
- Let's go and... - Shall we?

1207
00:43:23,317 --> 00:43:25,356
- Let's go and have some coffee. - Okay.

1208
00:43:25,357 --> 00:43:27,386
Let's have some coffee in Sogyeok-dong.

1209
00:43:27,387 --> 00:43:29,426
It tasted better because Soo Bin treated us.

1210
00:43:29,427 --> 00:43:30,456
- Thank you. - Thanks.

1211
00:43:30,457 --> 00:43:31,597
Thank you.

1212
00:43:32,467 --> 00:43:34,496
- It's a bit hot during the day. - Yes.

1213
00:43:34,497 --> 00:43:36,167
(They'll have coffee near the second spare time spot.)

1214
00:43:37,067 --> 00:43:39,107
I used to walk like this in the past.

1215
00:43:41,907 --> 00:43:44,076
- This was how people walked before. - That's right.

1216
00:43:44,077 --> 00:43:46,907
Yes. These days, people see it as the oldies' way.

1217
00:43:48,047 --> 00:43:49,916
There are memes like that.

1218
00:43:49,917 --> 00:43:52,147
- That's what I go after. - Right.

1219
00:43:52,287 --> 00:43:53,287
- Yes. - While holding a jacket, they go,

1220
00:43:53,288 --> 00:43:55,716
- "Hey, let's get ice pops." - Let's get ice pops.

1221
00:43:55,717 --> 00:43:58,086
- "Let's get twin ice pops." - We'd get an ice pop like this.

1222
00:43:58,087 --> 00:43:59,087
- Right. - Yes.

1223
00:43:59,088 --> 00:44:00,226
"Let's split the twin ice pop..."

1224
00:44:00,227 --> 00:44:01,956
"to see who's the lucky one." Something like that.

1225
00:44:01,957 --> 00:44:05,027
I aspire to be an old-timer.

1226
00:44:05,367 --> 00:44:06,726
- He goes for the oldie vibe. - Yes.

1227
00:44:06,727 --> 00:44:10,567
These days, the younger generation...

1228
00:44:10,797 --> 00:44:12,707
- finds oldies funny. - Yes.

1229
00:44:12,937 --> 00:44:14,707
You just wait five years.

1230
00:44:15,737 --> 00:44:16,977
You'll become the oldies right away.

1231
00:44:17,537 --> 00:44:19,206
- You'll be the old-timers. - After five years?

1232
00:44:19,207 --> 00:44:20,207
(The old-timer's precious advice)

1233
00:44:20,677 --> 00:44:23,447
At some point, I've become an old man,

1234
00:44:24,117 --> 00:44:25,787
- and I love it. - Do you?

1235
00:44:26,147 --> 00:44:29,056
- Don't be afraid, Seung Ho. - What do you like about it?

1236
00:44:29,057 --> 00:44:31,457
Well, it's nice. What's there not to like?

1237
00:44:31,857 --> 00:44:34,356
- Do you feel comfortable? - Yes. I feel comfortable.

1238
00:44:34,357 --> 00:44:36,127
Gosh. Hello. Yes.

1239
00:44:37,027 --> 00:44:39,796
- I like that I'm this carefree. - Actually, I don't mind...

1240
00:44:39,797 --> 00:44:41,726
- becoming an old man. - You don't.

1241
00:44:41,727 --> 00:44:43,536
I'm curious about what I'll be like in my 40s.

1242
00:44:43,537 --> 00:44:44,767
Really? I see.

1243
00:44:45,567 --> 00:44:46,767
Don't be afraid.

1244
00:44:47,237 --> 00:44:48,406
Soo Bin. Got it?

1245
00:44:48,407 --> 00:44:50,536
My friends call me C-Auntie.

1246
00:44:50,537 --> 00:44:52,046
- Really? - It's short for Celeb Auntie.

1247
00:44:52,047 --> 00:44:54,276
Good. That's nice.

1248
00:44:54,277 --> 00:44:55,376
Do we get on a bus here?

1249
00:44:55,377 --> 00:44:56,547
We'll take Bus Jongno 11.

1250
00:44:57,377 --> 00:44:58,617
It's Bus Jongno 11.

1251
00:44:59,417 --> 00:45:00,587
This one.

1252
00:45:00,847 --> 00:45:02,087
Okay. Bus Jongno 11?

1253
00:45:02,587 --> 00:45:04,216
We have to tap our card on the bus, right?

1254
00:45:04,217 --> 00:45:05,627
- I have the card. - I see.

1255
00:45:06,027 --> 00:45:08,856
In short, I'm getting a free ride today.

1256
00:45:08,857 --> 00:45:09,897
(Laughing)

1257
00:45:10,297 --> 00:45:13,097
I had coffee, thanks to the product placement.

1258
00:45:13,367 --> 00:45:14,927
Soo Bin paid for lunch.

1259
00:45:15,267 --> 00:45:18,167
Yeon Shik will pay the bus fare with his card.

1260
00:45:20,467 --> 00:45:22,076
Let's play a game for coffee.

1261
00:45:22,077 --> 00:45:24,177
- Let's do it. - Let's play it. Good.

1262
00:45:24,937 --> 00:45:26,007
Which game should we play?

1263
00:45:27,777 --> 00:45:29,377
First, we'll hold a piece of napkin together.

1264
00:45:29,747 --> 00:45:31,477
- And we tear it. - And we pull it.

1265
00:45:31,677 --> 00:45:33,516
- The one with... - The smallest piece is the loser.

1266
00:45:33,517 --> 00:45:35,187
- Let's go with that one. Yes. Good. - Yes. Sounds good.

1267
00:45:35,357 --> 00:45:37,587
- Good. - We'll hold each corner of it.

1268
00:45:38,527 --> 00:45:39,827
- That's it. - It's here.

1269
00:45:39,957 --> 00:45:41,787
- Where? - Bus 11 over there.

1270
00:45:42,197 --> 00:45:43,557
It's here.

1271
00:45:44,197 --> 00:45:45,297
The bus is packed.

1272
00:45:46,027 --> 00:45:48,067
I see. This is a popular line.

1273
00:45:48,397 --> 00:45:49,936
Gosh. Many people are getting on the bus.

1274
00:45:49,937 --> 00:45:51,367
This is a popular line.

1275
00:45:52,007 --> 00:45:53,206
Four adults, please.

1276
00:45:53,207 --> 00:45:54,337
Transaction completed.

1277
00:45:54,607 --> 00:45:55,906
More people are still getting on.

1278
00:45:55,907 --> 00:45:57,007
It's packed.

1279
00:45:58,137 --> 00:45:59,877
There's no space. Go inside.

1280
00:46:00,507 --> 00:46:02,677
- There's no space. - There's no room at the back.

1281
00:46:03,217 --> 00:46:04,376
- I'll go further in. - Okay.

1282
00:46:04,377 --> 00:46:05,387
(Squeezed in as tightly as possible)

1283
00:46:05,917 --> 00:46:07,446
- In the middle of the day... - It's been a while...

1284
00:46:07,447 --> 00:46:08,816
since you were on a packed bus, right?

1285
00:46:08,817 --> 00:46:09,956
It's been a really long while.

1286
00:46:09,957 --> 00:46:11,087
This is new.

1287
00:46:11,887 --> 00:46:12,926
You're too far away.

1288
00:46:12,927 --> 00:46:13,927
(The camera is really close as they're on a packed bus.)

1289
00:46:14,327 --> 00:46:15,797
(Laughing)

1290
00:46:15,957 --> 00:46:17,026
I mean...

1291
00:46:17,027 --> 00:46:18,597
Taking a cab might have been better.

1292
00:46:21,867 --> 00:46:24,896
We would've been able to talk if we were in a cab.

1293
00:46:24,897 --> 00:46:25,907
(Laughing)

1294
00:46:26,037 --> 00:46:27,366
Actually, it would've been better to walk.

1295
00:46:27,367 --> 00:46:28,507
(Laughing)

1296
00:46:30,307 --> 00:46:31,377
We could've walked.

1297
00:46:32,407 --> 00:46:33,646
(Stumbling as the bus turns)

1298
00:46:33,647 --> 00:46:34,906
- I'm sorry. - It's okay.

1299
00:46:34,907 --> 00:46:36,146
I'll stand firm for you.

1300
00:46:36,147 --> 00:46:37,217
(Laughing)

1301
00:46:38,347 --> 00:46:40,047
I don't think you can stand firm.

1302
00:46:40,217 --> 00:46:41,747
I kept him and Soo Bin...

1303
00:46:42,117 --> 00:46:43,387
- I kept them steady. - Really?

1304
00:46:43,757 --> 00:46:44,817
I stood still.

1305
00:46:45,157 --> 00:46:46,326
You lurched violently.

1306
00:46:46,327 --> 00:46:47,457
He's so funny.

1307
00:46:47,727 --> 00:46:49,927
- This is the golden line. - Right.

1308
00:46:50,227 --> 00:46:52,496
It goes deep into Samcheong-dong.

1309
00:46:52,497 --> 00:46:53,897
(Gwanghwamun Station- Gyeongbokgung Palace-Samcheong-dong line)

1310
00:46:54,067 --> 00:46:55,467
Gosh. They're getting off.

1311
00:46:57,067 --> 00:46:58,837
(The priority seat is empty.)

1312
00:46:59,037 --> 00:47:01,607
Jae Seok, sit in the seat for the elderly and the weak.

1313
00:47:03,177 --> 00:47:04,407
I can't really sit there.

1314
00:47:04,607 --> 00:47:05,747
It's a bit strange for me to sit there.

1315
00:47:06,707 --> 00:47:08,847
Come on. I don't really fit in there.

1316
00:47:08,977 --> 00:47:10,917
Among us, you're the only one who could sit there.

1317
00:47:11,047 --> 00:47:13,747
You're the closest one to suit the requirement.

1318
00:47:15,387 --> 00:47:17,387
Seung Ho. Why are you ignoring me?

1319
00:47:18,287 --> 00:47:20,887
I couldn't laugh at your face.

1320
00:47:21,957 --> 00:47:23,726
I'm strong. I am.

1321
00:47:23,727 --> 00:47:26,067
(I'm not the weak.)

1322
00:47:27,967 --> 00:47:29,237
People are up there too.

1323
00:47:30,097 --> 00:47:31,196
(It's still packed.)

1324
00:47:31,197 --> 00:47:32,437
They're standing up there.

1325
00:47:32,607 --> 00:47:33,607
(Bending over)

1326
00:47:33,608 --> 00:47:35,807
Gosh, Jae Seok. Don't come too close.

1327
00:47:36,637 --> 00:47:37,777
You're making me uncomfortable.

1328
00:47:40,047 --> 00:47:41,207
He startled me.

1329
00:47:41,407 --> 00:47:42,817
That was a bit dangerous.

1330
00:47:43,547 --> 00:47:46,847
If you get on a bus when you're in a situationship,

1331
00:47:47,317 --> 00:47:49,657
- I don't want to ride it with you. - I think it'll be great.

1332
00:47:50,587 --> 00:47:51,956
(The next spare time they're heading to...)

1333
00:47:51,957 --> 00:47:53,287
(while enjoying the situation ship is...)

1334
00:47:53,627 --> 00:47:55,397
- It's from Jang Yu Min. - Yu Min.

1335
00:47:55,727 --> 00:47:57,296
"To share the elegant melodies..."

1336
00:47:57,297 --> 00:47:59,827
"of the original K-culture,"

1337
00:48:00,097 --> 00:48:03,467
"I dress up every day and wait for students to come."

1338
00:48:03,897 --> 00:48:05,466
"I've mastered "Soda Pop..."

1339
00:48:05,467 --> 00:48:07,637
"and "Dynamite at an advanced age."

1340
00:48:07,837 --> 00:48:11,407
"But in reality, all I hear is the flies flying."

1341
00:48:13,277 --> 00:48:16,576
"Please fill up my schedule, which has plenty of spare time."

1342
00:48:16,577 --> 00:48:18,477
- I see. - I mean... It's...

1343
00:48:18,817 --> 00:48:22,417
- She teaches K-pop dance, but... - Right.

1344
00:48:22,687 --> 00:48:25,327
- She's welcoming new students, - Yes.

1345
00:48:25,427 --> 00:48:27,226
- but there is none. - You're right.

1346
00:48:27,227 --> 00:48:28,327
(Is it a K-pop dance academy?)

1347
00:48:28,997 --> 00:48:31,357
- This is where... - This is a hot spot.

1348
00:48:31,797 --> 00:48:33,766
For the tourists from overseas,

1349
00:48:33,767 --> 00:48:35,636
- this is a popular spot. - Jae Seok.

1350
00:48:35,637 --> 00:48:37,866
- It's like a cafe street. - Yes.

1351
00:48:37,867 --> 00:48:39,066
It's Samcheong-dong.

1352
00:48:39,067 --> 00:48:40,236
(The traditional charm meets modern style.)

1353
00:48:40,237 --> 00:48:43,607
She opened a dance academy in a prime location.

1354
00:48:43,707 --> 00:48:45,847
The academy should be thriving at a place like this.

1355
00:48:46,777 --> 00:48:49,017
- It's on the third floor. - On which building?

1356
00:48:50,077 --> 00:48:51,416
- Gosh. - Here?

1357
00:48:51,417 --> 00:48:52,517
It's here.

1358
00:48:53,517 --> 00:48:55,587
- What? Gayageum? - Gayageum?

1359
00:48:56,087 --> 00:48:57,987
- It says gayageum. - She teaches the gayageum.

1360
00:48:58,057 --> 00:48:59,757
Does she teach the gayageum, not the dance?

1361
00:48:59,887 --> 00:49:00,956
- Shall we? - Yes.

1362
00:49:00,957 --> 00:49:02,226
- Are we skipping coffee? - What?

1363
00:49:02,227 --> 00:49:03,256
Coffee?

1364
00:49:03,257 --> 00:49:05,497
Wait. We still have some time.

1365
00:49:05,727 --> 00:49:06,867
Right. Cafe? I see.

1366
00:49:07,167 --> 00:49:08,427
- Coffee. - It's at 1:30pm.

1367
00:49:09,097 --> 00:49:10,167
Let's have some coffee.

1368
00:49:10,537 --> 00:49:11,866
- I was going to get coffee, - Seung Ho...

1369
00:49:11,867 --> 00:49:13,167
but you said it was here.

1370
00:49:13,667 --> 00:49:16,277
- There should be many pretty cafes. - I was going to get it near here.

1371
00:49:16,737 --> 00:49:18,337
Shall we check out those places?

1372
00:49:18,637 --> 00:49:19,777
Where?

1373
00:49:20,247 --> 00:49:22,417
(Searching for a cafe)

1374
00:49:23,417 --> 00:49:24,546
What is it again?

1375
00:49:24,547 --> 00:49:26,116
- What are you doing, Seung Ho? - Why are you stretching your hips?

1376
00:49:26,117 --> 00:49:28,887
My hips are making a weird sound.

1377
00:49:29,357 --> 00:49:30,616
- What's going on? - Gosh.

1378
00:49:30,617 --> 00:49:32,127
It's okay. It's fixed now.

1379
00:49:32,357 --> 00:49:33,386
- Gosh. Seung Ho. - Are you all right?

1380
00:49:33,387 --> 00:49:34,487
Yes, I'm all right.

1381
00:49:35,557 --> 00:49:37,226
- Excuse me. - Hello.

1382
00:49:37,227 --> 00:49:38,356
Hello.

1383
00:49:38,357 --> 00:49:40,266
- Hello. - Gosh. I think it's Yu Jae Seok.

1384
00:49:40,267 --> 00:49:41,567
He has such a small face.

1385
00:49:41,997 --> 00:49:43,836
(Laughing)

1386
00:49:43,837 --> 00:49:46,537
Yu Jae Seok!

1387
00:49:46,867 --> 00:49:49,607
(Cheers from the excited ladies)

1388
00:49:50,077 --> 00:49:52,076
(He waves back.)

1389
00:49:52,077 --> 00:49:54,076
Gosh. Our aunties.

1390
00:49:54,077 --> 00:49:55,847
They're so...

1391
00:49:57,117 --> 00:49:58,117
Gosh. They're fierce.

1392
00:49:58,747 --> 00:50:01,947
They have to say something as they pass by.

1393
00:50:02,587 --> 00:50:03,617
That was hilarious.

1394
00:50:04,357 --> 00:50:06,486
- There's a cafe over here. - It's here.

1395
00:50:06,487 --> 00:50:07,627
- Gosh. It's here. - It's quiet.

1396
00:50:08,087 --> 00:50:10,527
- Hello. - Hello.

1397
00:50:10,897 --> 00:50:11,897
Welcome.

1398
00:50:12,127 --> 00:50:13,326
Gosh. What should I get?

1399
00:50:13,327 --> 00:50:14,327
(Looking around)

1400
00:50:15,067 --> 00:50:17,196
- Can I take a sheet of tissue? - Yes. You can take a lot.

1401
00:50:17,197 --> 00:50:18,467
- It's okay. - I just need one sheet.

1402
00:50:19,137 --> 00:50:20,636
I'll get an iced green tea.

1403
00:50:20,637 --> 00:50:22,207
- An iced green tea? Okay? - Please make it mild.

1404
00:50:23,937 --> 00:50:26,577
(He gets ready to play the game to pay for the coffee right away.)

1405
00:50:27,007 --> 00:50:28,276
Waid. Hold the corner.

1406
00:50:28,277 --> 00:50:29,646
Wait. We have to decide...

1407
00:50:29,647 --> 00:50:31,746
whether the one with the biggest piece or the smallest piece pays.

1408
00:50:31,747 --> 00:50:32,986
The smallest piece.

1409
00:50:32,987 --> 00:50:34,316
- The smallest piece? - Yes.

1410
00:50:34,317 --> 00:50:36,356
The one who has the smallest piece will pay for coffee.

1411
00:50:36,357 --> 00:50:37,786
Do we pull on the count of three?

1412
00:50:37,787 --> 00:50:38,827
- Wait. - What?

1413
00:50:41,287 --> 00:50:42,996
(Clearly, he has the tiniest piece.)

1414
00:50:42,997 --> 00:50:44,327
- On the count of three? What? - Wait.

1415
00:50:46,227 --> 00:50:48,866
- We have to do it again. - No, it's him.

1416
00:50:48,867 --> 00:50:50,736
- He has to buy. - It's okay.

1417
00:50:50,737 --> 00:50:51,867
(Seung Ho has to pay.)

1418
00:50:52,967 --> 00:50:54,006
Seung Ho.

1419
00:50:54,007 --> 00:50:55,106
(The fate was decided in an instant.)

1420
00:50:55,107 --> 00:50:56,207
(Go ahead and pay for it.)

1421
00:50:56,277 --> 00:50:57,836
I'll get an iced green tea.

1422
00:50:57,837 --> 00:50:59,206
Is the chocolate latte...

1423
00:50:59,207 --> 00:51:01,106
- Please make it sweet. Yes. - Do you want it sweet?

1424
00:51:01,107 --> 00:51:02,547
I'll get an iced milk tea.

1425
00:51:02,747 --> 00:51:04,777
- I'll get an iced vanilla latte. - Okay.

1426
00:51:05,787 --> 00:51:07,647
You're getting treated by the younger ones.

1427
00:51:09,017 --> 00:51:10,287
It happens sometimes.

1428
00:51:12,017 --> 00:51:13,427
- Thanks, Seung Ho. - Sure.

1429
00:51:13,827 --> 00:51:15,157
- Thanks, Seung Ho. - Thanks.

1430
00:51:15,997 --> 00:51:18,497
- I ordered a green tea. - There's one upstairs too.

1431
00:51:18,527 --> 00:51:19,667
Okay. Thanks.

1432
00:51:20,697 --> 00:51:21,826
Thank you, Seung Ho.

1433
00:51:21,827 --> 00:51:23,496
- Seung Ho. Thanks. - It's nothing.

1434
00:51:23,497 --> 00:51:24,537
Yes.

1435
00:51:24,597 --> 00:51:26,767
I don't know if I can say this, but you got off cheap.

1436
00:51:29,407 --> 00:51:30,636
Because we're full,

1437
00:51:30,637 --> 00:51:32,507
- Right. - we didn't order desserts.

1438
00:51:33,007 --> 00:51:34,907
- I agree that I got off cheap. - Yes.

1439
00:51:36,317 --> 00:51:39,216
These days, lunch costs...

1440
00:51:39,217 --> 00:51:40,517
about 10 or 12 dollars.

1441
00:51:40,887 --> 00:51:42,757
- Nothing's under ten dollars. - Nothing.

1442
00:51:43,287 --> 00:51:46,027
And Kwang Soo gets paid five dollars for his Bubble?

1443
00:51:47,987 --> 00:51:49,657
I can't believe that guy.

1444
00:51:49,897 --> 00:51:52,866
- That money doesn't go to him. - It's not for him.

1445
00:51:52,867 --> 00:51:55,366
- I have my own Bubble account too. - I see.

1446
00:51:55,367 --> 00:51:56,936
When I launch the app...

1447
00:51:56,937 --> 00:51:58,697
- to talk to my fans, - Yes.

1448
00:51:58,967 --> 00:52:00,607
the notification from Kwang Soo keeps popping up.

1449
00:52:01,507 --> 00:52:04,077
I pushed the "Don't show it for a week" button.

1450
00:52:04,437 --> 00:52:07,607
"Never show it again." Or something like that.

1451
00:52:08,147 --> 00:52:09,576
"Stop showing the message."

1452
00:52:09,577 --> 00:52:10,916
- Did you push that button? - I checked the mark,

1453
00:52:10,917 --> 00:52:12,146
but the notification kept coming.

1454
00:52:12,147 --> 00:52:13,747
(He gets to know how he's doing even if he doesn't want to.)

1455
00:52:13,847 --> 00:52:16,386
Was it a dance academy or a gayageum academy?

1456
00:52:16,387 --> 00:52:17,916
- Gayageum. - It was a gayageum academy.

1457
00:52:17,917 --> 00:52:19,827
I learned how to play it when I was young.

1458
00:52:19,887 --> 00:52:21,186
- Yes? - I see.

1459
00:52:21,187 --> 00:52:22,256
Was it for a hobby?

1460
00:52:22,257 --> 00:52:24,826
I learned it as a hobby when I was a sixth grader.

1461
00:52:24,827 --> 00:52:27,126
And to make it my skill when I applied to colleges,

1462
00:52:27,127 --> 00:52:28,597
I learned it again.

1463
00:52:28,667 --> 00:52:30,067
- Did you utilize that skill? - I did.

1464
00:52:30,237 --> 00:52:31,666
I played it while playing Hwang Jin Yi to enter college.

1465
00:52:31,667 --> 00:52:32,836
(She used her skills when playing Hwang Jin Yi.)

1466
00:52:32,837 --> 00:52:35,006
While playing the role of Hwang Jin Yi?

1467
00:52:35,007 --> 00:52:37,606
- For the free-choice performance. - You mixed it into the performance.

1468
00:52:37,607 --> 00:52:38,607
Yes.

1469
00:52:38,777 --> 00:52:41,077
If Soo Bin played Hwang Jin Yi,

1470
00:52:41,607 --> 00:52:43,176
she would've pulled it off well.

1471
00:52:43,177 --> 00:52:44,546
(She's perfect for the role.)

1472
00:52:44,547 --> 00:52:45,987
I'm sorry, but it's 1:30pm.

1473
00:52:46,347 --> 00:52:47,446
- Wait. We have to go. - Then we have to go.

1474
00:52:47,447 --> 00:52:48,517
Let's go.

1475
00:52:49,387 --> 00:52:51,017
Seung Ho and Soo Bin. Today,

1476
00:52:51,317 --> 00:52:52,827
- you treated us well. - The younger ones are the best.

1477
00:52:53,987 --> 00:52:57,697
(The two younger ones are on the street already.)

1478
00:52:58,927 --> 00:52:59,967
This is cute.

1479
00:53:01,397 --> 00:53:03,097
Which one is cuter between these two?

1480
00:53:03,937 --> 00:53:05,136
(The two are immersed in cute items.)

1481
00:53:05,137 --> 00:53:06,207
This one.

1482
00:53:08,867 --> 00:53:10,577
- Hello. - Hi.

1483
00:53:11,077 --> 00:53:12,777
They even have Monchhichi.

1484
00:53:12,907 --> 00:53:14,647
Gosh, it's Garyu Kitty.

1485
00:53:17,077 --> 00:53:18,416
- What's that? - What?

1486
00:53:18,417 --> 00:53:19,746
- This is it. - Seung Ho.

1487
00:53:19,747 --> 00:53:21,516
- It's 1:30pm. Where are you? - We have to hurry.

1488
00:53:21,517 --> 00:53:23,757
- Jae Seok, buy me this. - Get me this, Jae Seok.

1489
00:53:24,957 --> 00:53:26,027
Really?

1490
00:53:26,787 --> 00:53:28,527
Well. Yeon Seok too.

1491
00:53:29,097 --> 00:53:30,927
- Okay. Get them. - Which one should I get?

1492
00:53:31,027 --> 00:53:32,027
I should buy them for you.

1493
00:53:32,028 --> 00:53:33,197
- Hello. - Nice.

1494
00:53:33,527 --> 00:53:34,897
This one is really cute.

1495
00:53:36,397 --> 00:53:37,437
It's really cute.

1496
00:53:37,867 --> 00:53:39,006
(Soo Bin can't take her eyes off it.)

1497
00:53:39,007 --> 00:53:40,267
Get whatever you want.

1498
00:53:40,937 --> 00:53:43,176
- Like I was shot - Can I get these two?

1499
00:53:43,177 --> 00:53:44,737
- You can get two. - Yes.

1500
00:53:45,137 --> 00:53:46,277
Aren't you going to choose one?

1501
00:53:46,407 --> 00:53:48,777
- Why don't you... - Is this camera for sale?

1502
00:53:48,977 --> 00:53:50,717
- No. - It's not for sale.

1503
00:53:50,817 --> 00:53:52,276
(Sadly, he fails to make him pay big.)

1504
00:53:52,277 --> 00:53:54,647
- That camera is my style. - What are you doing?

1505
00:53:55,517 --> 00:53:57,716
- Did you pick one? - Can I buy an accessory?

1506
00:53:57,717 --> 00:53:58,787
Yes, you can.

1507
00:53:59,457 --> 00:54:02,227
But listen, Seung Ho.

1508
00:54:03,057 --> 00:54:04,157
You only...

1509
00:54:04,627 --> 00:54:07,867
- It's hard to pick one. - You only bought me a green tea.

1510
00:54:09,467 --> 00:54:10,666
Gosh. This is it.

1511
00:54:10,667 --> 00:54:11,997
(He doesn't care at all.)

1512
00:54:12,297 --> 00:54:14,307
This is it. Or this one?

1513
00:54:14,437 --> 00:54:16,137
It's all silver.

1514
00:54:16,337 --> 00:54:17,406
But here's the thing.

1515
00:54:17,407 --> 00:54:18,537
(Laughing)

1516
00:54:19,047 --> 00:54:21,507
- I mean, as for Soo Bin, - Yes.

1517
00:54:21,807 --> 00:54:23,647
she paid quite a bit for lunch.

1518
00:54:24,247 --> 00:54:25,417
But you only bought a green tea.

1519
00:54:27,787 --> 00:54:29,757
- This is it. - Bang, bang, bang

1520
00:54:30,217 --> 00:54:31,756
I do feel like I was shot.

1521
00:54:31,757 --> 00:54:32,787
(He's getting robbed after getting shot.)

1522
00:54:32,887 --> 00:54:34,726
- Thank you. - You're welcome.

1523
00:54:34,727 --> 00:54:36,696
- Thank you. - Thank you.

1524
00:54:36,697 --> 00:54:37,926
- Thank you. Have a good day. - Thank you.

1525
00:54:37,927 --> 00:54:39,297
- Thank you. - Have a good day.

1526
00:54:40,197 --> 00:54:41,267
It's right over here.

1527
00:54:42,327 --> 00:54:44,336
- Let's pull it off this time. - Let's do this.

1528
00:54:44,337 --> 00:54:46,436
- We have to make it happen. - Let's really do this.

1529
00:54:46,437 --> 00:54:48,837
- It's on the third floor. - She teaches the gayageum.

1530
00:54:49,437 --> 00:54:51,077
- Hello, ma'am. - Goodness.

1531
00:54:51,877 --> 00:54:52,906
- Hello. - Hi.

1532
00:54:52,907 --> 00:54:54,046
- Is this... - Hello.

1533
00:54:54,047 --> 00:54:55,277
- a gayageum academy? - Hello.

1534
00:54:55,407 --> 00:54:57,147
Gosh. Hello. Yes, it is.

1535
00:54:57,277 --> 00:54:58,916
- Is it a gayageum academy? - Yes, it is.

1536
00:54:58,917 --> 00:55:00,986
- Where should we sit? - Please come this way.

1537
00:55:00,987 --> 00:55:02,146
Gosh. This place is so pretty.

1538
00:55:02,147 --> 00:55:03,617
(Jang Yu Min, today's second Whenever Guest)

1539
00:55:03,857 --> 00:55:05,586
Gosh. Nice to meet you all.

1540
00:55:05,587 --> 00:55:06,687
Nice to meet you too.

1541
00:55:08,057 --> 00:55:10,296
- How's your health? - Pardon?

1542
00:55:10,297 --> 00:55:11,397
Right. I'm all right.

1543
00:55:11,827 --> 00:55:14,197
- His health. - It's been like this all day.

1544
00:55:14,827 --> 00:55:17,566
- It was nothing. Really. - I see.

1545
00:55:17,567 --> 00:55:18,737
Yes.

1546
00:55:18,897 --> 00:55:21,507
But the news sounded af if I fainted.

1547
00:55:21,867 --> 00:55:24,537
- Anyway, nice to meet you. - Nice to meet you.

1548
00:55:24,737 --> 00:55:26,206
Actually, we've...

1549
00:55:26,207 --> 00:55:28,876
We've come here after reading your letter.

1550
00:55:28,877 --> 00:55:31,046
- You said, "KPop Demon Hunters." - Yes.

1551
00:55:31,047 --> 00:55:34,186
So we thought you ran a dance studio.

1552
00:55:34,187 --> 00:55:35,387
I see. Right.

1553
00:55:35,957 --> 00:55:38,116
- But this is a gayageum academy. - It is.

1554
00:55:38,117 --> 00:55:39,187
- I see. - Yes.

1555
00:55:39,287 --> 00:55:41,527
Are there many students?

1556
00:55:41,757 --> 00:55:45,767
- I offer one-day classes. - I see.

1557
00:55:45,897 --> 00:55:49,697
When tourists come here,

1558
00:55:49,837 --> 00:55:51,497
I dress them up in hanbok.

1559
00:55:51,967 --> 00:55:55,207
And I teach them how to play "Arirang."

1560
00:55:55,337 --> 00:55:56,836
And you take photos for them too.

1561
00:55:56,837 --> 00:55:58,536
I take photos for them...

1562
00:55:58,537 --> 00:56:00,207
- to commemorate the moment. - I see.

1563
00:56:01,477 --> 00:56:03,516
(Whenever Guest)

1564
00:56:03,517 --> 00:56:07,017
(The one-day class is held in English.)

1565
00:56:08,317 --> 00:56:10,616
I teach them about the history of gayageum...

1566
00:56:10,617 --> 00:56:12,556
that it's a traditional Korean instrument.

1567
00:56:12,557 --> 00:56:13,557
(Teaching the gayageum's history and how to play it)

1568
00:56:13,627 --> 00:56:15,656
You're going global with people from around the world.

1569
00:56:15,657 --> 00:56:18,396
- Yes. - It's because the interest...

1570
00:56:18,397 --> 00:56:20,666
- in Korean culture's been growing. - Yes.

1571
00:56:20,667 --> 00:56:22,696
Will you play a song...

1572
00:56:22,697 --> 00:56:24,596
- from "KPop Demon Hunters?" - I know. Will you play it?

1573
00:56:24,597 --> 00:56:25,666
- We want to hear it. - Please.

1574
00:56:25,667 --> 00:56:27,436
Like "Soda Pop" from "KPop Demon Hunters?"

1575
00:56:27,437 --> 00:56:28,667
- "Soda Pop" sounds good. - Okay.

1576
00:56:29,107 --> 00:56:30,137
It goes like this.

1577
00:56:33,577 --> 00:56:35,647
- It's "Soda Pop." - Yes.

1578
00:56:35,947 --> 00:56:38,447
Soda pop

1579
00:56:39,217 --> 00:56:40,317
That's it.

1580
00:56:40,947 --> 00:56:42,656
- Yes. We play that one. - You can play it with the gayageum.

1581
00:56:42,657 --> 00:56:45,057
- What else can you play? - The songs by BTS.

1582
00:56:45,257 --> 00:56:47,456
- People love "Dynamite." - Actually,

1583
00:56:47,457 --> 00:56:49,926
overall, you pick the songs...

1584
00:56:49,927 --> 00:56:51,056
- the foreigners love. - That foreigners would know.

1585
00:56:51,057 --> 00:56:52,057
- You focus on those. - K-pop songs.

1586
00:56:52,058 --> 00:56:55,097
- Yes. Here's "Dynamite." - "Dynamite."

1587
00:56:56,697 --> 00:56:58,666
- Dynamite - There you go.

1588
00:56:58,667 --> 00:57:00,067
(Joining the chorus)

1589
00:57:05,207 --> 00:57:06,207
(Hesitating)

1590
00:57:08,407 --> 00:57:10,377
Dynamite. It works perfectly.

1591
00:57:10,947 --> 00:57:11,947
(Satisfied with the gayageum accompaniment)

1592
00:57:11,948 --> 00:57:13,616
- It works perfectly, doesn't it? - Yes.

1593
00:57:13,617 --> 00:57:16,256
- Anything other than K-pop? - Yes.

1594
00:57:16,257 --> 00:57:18,216
- Anything traditional like gukak? - Yes.

1595
00:57:18,217 --> 00:57:19,856
Can you perform one of those?

1596
00:57:19,857 --> 00:57:21,527
(What about the scores among traditional gukak?)

1597
00:57:21,627 --> 00:57:23,356
- Scores like "Gayageum Sanjo." - Yes.

1598
00:57:23,357 --> 00:57:25,726
- "Gayageum Sanjo." - Yes. Foreigners love...

1599
00:57:25,727 --> 00:57:28,526
- scores like that. And so do I. - I see.

1600
00:57:28,527 --> 00:57:29,997
- Really? - Yes.

1601
00:57:30,197 --> 00:57:32,137
- Will you play it for us? - Gayageum is...

1602
00:57:32,767 --> 00:57:34,267
I haven't practiced it for a while.

1603
00:57:34,367 --> 00:57:36,507
You can play K-pop songs, but not traditional gukak?

1604
00:57:36,937 --> 00:57:38,976
- I'll try it. - Goodness.

1605
00:57:38,977 --> 00:57:41,676
She could play K-pop songs without a problem.

1606
00:57:41,677 --> 00:57:42,717
I'll give it a go.

1607
00:57:48,117 --> 00:57:50,857
(The gayageum's clear melody rings through the air.)

1608
00:57:51,687 --> 00:57:53,887
(This is it!)

1609
00:58:00,567 --> 00:58:04,667
(The bouncy melody blooms at her fingertips.)

1610
00:58:14,947 --> 00:58:16,816
(Amazed)

1611
00:58:16,817 --> 00:58:18,046
It was beautiful.

1612
00:58:18,047 --> 00:58:20,786
Gosh. K-pop songs are great too,

1613
00:58:20,787 --> 00:58:22,286
- but this is it. - This one beats them. Yes.

1614
00:58:22,287 --> 00:58:23,657
- Yes. - "Gayageum Sanjo" is the best.

1615
00:58:24,287 --> 00:58:26,226
- Now, Soo Bin will play it. - Yes.

1616
00:58:26,227 --> 00:58:28,086
- Hold it the other way. - I...

1617
00:58:28,087 --> 00:58:30,356
It's been about ten years, though.

1618
00:58:30,357 --> 00:58:32,026
- I can't really remember. - Soo Bin will play it too.

1619
00:58:32,027 --> 00:58:33,296
- Soo Bin. - Play a K-pop song.

1620
00:58:33,297 --> 00:58:34,397
I want to see you play it.

1621
00:58:35,297 --> 00:58:37,137
Play the score you're familiar with.

1622
00:58:37,367 --> 00:58:38,397
Is there a song you know?

1623
00:58:38,937 --> 00:58:40,437
This is what I remember from then.

1624
00:58:48,747 --> 00:58:51,147
(Her fingers move fearlessly even though it's been a while.)

1625
00:58:52,817 --> 00:58:53,987
- She's quite good. - Something like this.

1626
00:58:55,487 --> 00:58:56,557
Soo Bin.

1627
00:58:56,987 --> 00:58:58,756
(Amazed)

1628
00:58:58,757 --> 00:59:00,686
- Soo Bin. Thanks to this shot, - Yes.

1629
00:59:00,687 --> 00:59:02,027
you'll get a role in a historic drama.

1630
00:59:02,827 --> 00:59:03,997
Wait and see.

1631
00:59:04,557 --> 00:59:06,967
- You'll get a role right away. - They'll offer you a role.

1632
00:59:07,897 --> 00:59:08,897
Why don't you try it, Jae Seok?

1633
00:59:09,497 --> 00:59:11,467
- Me? Well... - Play "Arirang."

1634
00:59:12,037 --> 00:59:13,136
- "Arirang?" - Yes.

1635
00:59:13,137 --> 00:59:14,406
- I've never played it before. - Learn it.

1636
00:59:14,407 --> 00:59:16,107
Start from this string.

1637
00:59:16,407 --> 00:59:18,307
When you pluck the strings in this order, it's "Arirang."

1638
00:59:21,447 --> 00:59:24,577
(Plucking each string, following her instruction)

1639
00:59:30,287 --> 00:59:32,187
- Yes. - This is the one-day class.

1640
00:59:33,557 --> 00:59:35,027
- This is how you do it. - A little bit.

1641
00:59:35,427 --> 00:59:37,756
- You push down the strings. - I mean, that was...

1642
00:59:37,757 --> 00:59:39,796
That's what the one-day class is like.

1643
00:59:39,797 --> 00:59:42,226
But it's more...

1644
00:59:42,227 --> 00:59:44,636
- You teach them in more detail. - Yes.

1645
00:59:44,637 --> 00:59:47,137
The lesson wasn't detailed because I didn't pay.

1646
00:59:47,537 --> 00:59:49,437
- So that's it. Once you pay... - No. We were just out of time.

1647
00:59:49,777 --> 00:59:52,336
When we have more time, we can take the one-day class.

1648
00:59:52,337 --> 00:59:53,476
- Yes. - I got it.

1649
00:59:53,477 --> 00:59:55,607
It must be a great memory for the customers...

1650
00:59:55,807 --> 00:59:58,446
- Yes. - who are here for a trip.

1651
00:59:58,447 --> 01:00:01,847
In the letter you sent us,

1652
01:00:02,447 --> 01:00:04,156
- you said you were struggling. - Yes.

1653
01:00:04,157 --> 01:00:05,556
(Is she having a hard time lately?)

1654
01:00:05,557 --> 01:00:06,687
How is it going?

1655
01:00:06,987 --> 01:00:10,596
Actually, for a long time,

1656
01:00:10,597 --> 01:00:12,897
- I ran an academy in Goyang. - I see

1657
01:00:13,097 --> 01:00:14,996
- Yes. I taught students. - Right.

1658
01:00:14,997 --> 01:00:17,266
Then I ambitiously moved to Bukchon...

1659
01:00:17,267 --> 01:00:20,066
- to do something with foreigners. - I see.

1660
01:00:20,067 --> 01:00:22,166
That was how it got started.

1661
01:00:22,167 --> 01:00:25,306
- But this was a new type of work. - I see.

1662
01:00:25,307 --> 01:00:28,076
There are so many people walking around here.

1663
01:00:28,077 --> 01:00:29,476
The thing is,

1664
01:00:29,477 --> 01:00:32,746
these streets are packed with people.

1665
01:00:32,747 --> 01:00:34,717
Yes. What makes me saddest...

1666
01:00:35,787 --> 01:00:37,656
is when there are so many foreigners out there,

1667
01:00:37,657 --> 01:00:40,687
but I am sitting here alone without any reservations.

1668
01:00:41,327 --> 01:00:42,957
(Sad)

1669
01:00:43,727 --> 01:00:46,797
I practice by myself while looking at the mountains.

1670
01:00:48,067 --> 01:00:49,696
(The view with tears in her eyes)

1671
01:00:49,697 --> 01:00:52,137
The view is amazing,

1672
01:00:52,497 --> 01:00:53,937
- Exactly. - but...

1673
01:00:54,337 --> 01:00:56,936
You need more visitors.

1674
01:00:56,937 --> 01:00:59,446
Did anyone make reservations after this?

1675
01:00:59,447 --> 01:01:01,147
- Tomorrow. - Tomorrow?

1676
01:01:01,777 --> 01:01:02,946
Did you free up your schedule...

1677
01:01:02,947 --> 01:01:04,117
- for us? - Of course.

1678
01:01:06,347 --> 01:01:09,416
- She freed it up on purpose. - Yes.

1679
01:01:09,417 --> 01:01:11,657
- It was to shoot our show. - For the shoot.

1680
01:01:12,887 --> 01:01:14,956
I couldn't pay rent last year...

1681
01:01:14,957 --> 01:01:16,156
- because I was in the red. - Right.

1682
01:01:16,157 --> 01:01:18,226
This year, thanks to BTS...

1683
01:01:18,227 --> 01:01:19,796
- It's become better. - Yes.

1684
01:01:19,797 --> 01:01:22,497
They had concerts in Korea.

1685
01:01:23,067 --> 01:01:24,737
- They made a comeback in March. - Yes.

1686
01:01:27,467 --> 01:01:30,176
When they had their concerts in Goyang back in April,

1687
01:01:30,177 --> 01:01:32,336
- some ARMYs came here. - They did.

1688
01:01:32,337 --> 01:01:34,476
When BTS had their Busan concerts in June,

1689
01:01:34,477 --> 01:01:35,876
- they came. - They did.

1690
01:01:35,877 --> 01:01:37,446
- So, we can say... - June was great.

1691
01:01:37,447 --> 01:01:39,446
- that BTS's concerts... - Yes.

1692
01:01:39,447 --> 01:01:41,847
- decide the fate of this place. - They're connected.

1693
01:01:42,047 --> 01:01:46,016
The number of your customers rises accordingly.

1694
01:01:46,017 --> 01:01:47,727
- Yes, that's right. - I see.

1695
01:01:48,257 --> 01:01:50,296
Good. Since we're here...

1696
01:01:50,297 --> 01:01:53,666
We unfortunately failed before we came here.

1697
01:01:53,667 --> 01:01:56,026
If we fail again at this place, we'll push her...

1698
01:01:56,027 --> 01:02:00,207
- into deeper depression. - Gosh. Right.

1699
01:02:01,067 --> 01:02:02,537
- Let me put this at the back. - Okay.

1700
01:02:03,207 --> 01:02:04,377
I'll do it for you.

1701
01:02:04,537 --> 01:02:06,306
- Yes. - It's okay, though.

1702
01:02:06,307 --> 01:02:07,307
(Kind)

1703
01:02:07,308 --> 01:02:08,507
Thank you.

1704
01:02:08,807 --> 01:02:09,817
(Thud)

1705
01:02:11,747 --> 01:02:13,287
(Surprised)

1706
01:02:16,317 --> 01:02:18,117
- Was it on purpose? - I'm sorry.

1707
01:02:18,587 --> 01:02:21,887
- You did it on purpose, didn't you? - Gosh. No.

1708
01:02:22,927 --> 01:02:24,327
- It's all right. - I'm sorry.

1709
01:02:24,527 --> 01:02:28,226
I'm sorry for keeping you waiting for a week too.

1710
01:02:28,227 --> 01:02:30,067
- It's okay. - My apologies.

1711
01:02:32,597 --> 01:02:36,207
(Opening for the first present after calming down)

1712
01:02:36,607 --> 01:02:38,576
"This goes well with our graceful hanbok."

1713
01:02:38,577 --> 01:02:40,506
"It'll brighten up your skin."

1714
01:02:40,507 --> 01:02:42,246
"Chanel skincare set."

1715
01:02:42,247 --> 01:02:43,247
(Round 1 present: Chanel skincare set)

1716
01:02:43,248 --> 01:02:45,247
A Chanel skincare set. Goodness.

1717
01:02:50,417 --> 01:02:51,816
Gosh, ma'am.

1718
01:02:51,817 --> 01:02:53,756
- Yes. - It's a skincare set.

1719
01:02:53,757 --> 01:02:55,086
- I love it. - Yes.

1720
01:02:55,087 --> 01:02:58,196
(Sogo Bounce!)

1721
01:02:58,197 --> 01:02:59,966
(Pass the table tennis ball by bouncing it on the sogo.)

1722
01:02:59,967 --> 01:03:02,696
(The last player has to put the ball into gat, the triditional hat.)

1723
01:03:02,697 --> 01:03:05,037
(Round 1: A round trip)

1724
01:03:05,137 --> 01:03:06,767
- In the gat while seated? - Yes.

1725
01:03:07,367 --> 01:03:09,406
We bounce the ball on the sogo, right?

1726
01:03:09,407 --> 01:03:11,836
- We do it like this. - We pass it from over there.

1727
01:03:11,837 --> 01:03:13,107
Make a round trip.

1728
01:03:13,347 --> 01:03:15,746
- It's a round trip. - It has to go back.

1729
01:03:15,747 --> 01:03:16,776
(The ball has to reach the end and come back.)

1730
01:03:16,777 --> 01:03:18,846
- Can we bounce it multiple times? - We can do it as much as we want?

1731
01:03:18,847 --> 01:03:20,447
- Is there a time limit? - No.

1732
01:03:21,147 --> 01:03:22,247
Let's try it.

1733
01:03:23,687 --> 01:03:25,087
Tell me before you pass it.

1734
01:03:26,117 --> 01:03:28,457
- Okay. I'll get it right away. - You just have to get it.

1735
01:03:29,627 --> 01:03:30,727
Here.

1736
01:03:31,857 --> 01:03:32,927
I'll pass it.

1737
01:03:35,067 --> 01:03:36,436
- Hey. - I know.

1738
01:03:36,437 --> 01:03:38,097
- You really have to bounce it. - Gosh. This is...

1739
01:03:38,837 --> 01:03:39,906
Here.

1740
01:03:39,907 --> 01:03:40,907
(Practicing again)

1741
01:03:42,107 --> 01:03:43,107
Here.

1742
01:03:46,677 --> 01:03:48,147
Your mother plays tennis.

1743
01:03:49,817 --> 01:03:50,977
- She's good at it, right? - Yes.

1744
01:03:51,977 --> 01:03:53,586
- Let's do this. - Go, everyone.

1745
01:03:53,587 --> 01:03:55,017
- I have to keep going like this. - Okay.

1746
01:03:55,717 --> 01:03:56,756
Here.

1747
01:03:56,757 --> 01:03:57,917
(A fresh start)

1748
01:03:58,217 --> 01:03:59,316
- Pass it. - Here. No.

1749
01:03:59,317 --> 01:04:01,157
- Again. I'll pass it again. - Pass it to her.

1750
01:04:01,427 --> 01:04:03,527
- I'll do it again. - Hey.

1751
01:04:04,257 --> 01:04:06,827
Hold on. Soo Bin.

1752
01:04:07,267 --> 01:04:08,366
(They have a major weak link.)

1753
01:04:08,367 --> 01:04:09,466
Soo Bin isn't good at this.

1754
01:04:09,467 --> 01:04:10,696
- Then... - Should I go first?

1755
01:04:10,697 --> 01:04:11,996
Hold on. I think...

1756
01:04:11,997 --> 01:04:13,636
- Soo Bin should... No. - She should go first.

1757
01:04:13,637 --> 01:04:15,007
She should make the U-turn.

1758
01:04:15,507 --> 01:04:16,707
- What? - Otherwise, she has to play twice.

1759
01:04:17,277 --> 01:04:19,036
You two should switch places.

1760
01:04:19,037 --> 01:04:21,007
- Really? That's true. - Right. Or I need to make the goal.

1761
01:04:21,047 --> 01:04:23,517
She has to play twice and make a goal if she goes first.

1762
01:04:23,717 --> 01:04:24,917
- Good. - Good luck.

1763
01:04:25,117 --> 01:04:26,247
- Let's go. - Okay.

1764
01:04:26,847 --> 01:04:30,117
Try bouncing it a few times by yourself, Soo Bin.

1765
01:04:33,027 --> 01:04:35,587
- Soo Bin. - It was rolling.

1766
01:04:36,157 --> 01:04:37,227
Are you making fried eggs?

1767
01:04:38,857 --> 01:04:40,266
You have to snap your wrist...

1768
01:04:40,267 --> 01:04:41,626
- with confidence. - Okay.

1769
01:04:41,627 --> 01:04:42,967
- How do I do it? - Give it to me.

1770
01:04:43,537 --> 01:04:44,666
Snap it harder.

1771
01:04:44,667 --> 01:04:45,797
(Snapping my wrist?)

1772
01:04:46,067 --> 01:04:47,337
Wake up, Soo Bin.

1773
01:04:49,407 --> 01:04:50,476
What do we do with her?

1774
01:04:50,477 --> 01:04:51,536
(Super worried)

1775
01:04:51,537 --> 01:04:53,546
- Soo Bin! - Do it gently like this, Soo Bin.

1776
01:04:53,547 --> 01:04:55,947
- Bounce it on the floor first. - Okay.

1777
01:05:00,047 --> 01:05:01,187
